/**
 * Every clip must be a `completed` video job of this campaign, else 422 `clip_not_completed` naming it. A clip whose
 * latest QC is `failed` or `skipped` must be listed in `confirmations.qcOverride`, else 422
 * `qc_confirmation_required` naming it; the confirmation is recorded (`qcOverrideConfirmed=true`). A clip whose latest
 * QC is `pending` needs no confirmation (QC never blocks assembly) and is stored with `qcOverrideConfirmed=false`
 * (TD-D36). A `qcOverride` ID that is not in `clips` is 400 `validation_failed` with `details[].path`
 * `confirmations.qcOverride[i]`, and nothing is created. A `qcOverride` ID for a clip whose latest QC is `passed` or
 * `pending` when the request commits is accepted and ignored: no confirmation is recorded and that clip's
 * `qcOverrideConfirmed` is false (TD-D35). QC state is read inside the create transaction. Only a new row counts toward
 * ASSEMBLY_RENDERS_PER_USER_PER_DAY (UTC day); the 21st gets 422 `assembly_daily_limit`.
 * @summary Assemble chosen completed clips in order (reuse; daily render limit)
 */
